Post-stratification weighting is often (but not always) a component of the weights accompanying survey data - see here  <http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/weightingfinal.pdf>for distinction. I'm specifically thinking about simulating quantities from the model for a different distribution of covariates.

Examples:
http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/survey_methodology.pdf
http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/Si_et_al-BA14.pdf
http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/KennedyGelman_manuscript.pdf
http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/improving_mrp.pdf
https://www.cambridge.org/core/membership/services/aop-file-manager/file/5c2f6ebb7cf9ee1118d11c0a/APMM-2019-Simon-Jackman.pdf

Cheers,

Brett

