In blavaan you cannot add any type of weights. There are some discussions about qhet does it mean to add weights in MCMC estimation and posterior distributions in the Stan forum https://discourse.mc-stan.org/search?q=sampling%20weights

You could get the posterior distribution from a model, and then adjust it by weights, maybe?

>From this " I'm specifically thinking about simulating quantities from the model for a different distribution of covariates. ", not sure you would need weights. What type of simulation are you thinking? Can you give me a more specific process what this looks like?
Because you can use simulate data with blavaan based on the estimated posteriors, or you can also simulate data set with the simsem package, and based this on the posterior means of blavaan

